# Recorded by hand from a reference runtime; see docs/reference-runtime.md.
# The model this refers to is NOT committed -- see docs/fixture-provenance.md
# for where to obtain it. No mandatory test reads this file.
#
# Tokenization came from:
#   llama-tokenize -m tinyllama-q8_0.gguf -p "The capital of France is" --ids
#     -> [1, 450, 7483, 310, 3444, 338]
#
# Greedy continuation came from llama-cli with --temp 0, which printed
#   "The capital of France is Paris."
# for the same prompt, so the continuation is " Paris." -- the leading space
# belongs to the token and is written here as the \s escape because the
# directive value is trimmed.

runtime llama.cpp b1-717dad5
model tinyllama-1.1b-chat-v1.0.Q8_0.gguf
prompt The capital of France is
tokens 1 450 7483 310 3444 338
greedy_text \sParis.

# Three logits at the position after the prompt, from llama-eval-callback,
# which prints the first three and last three values of result_output. The
# tolerance is 0.08 because that is what the two implementations agree to,
# not because it is what anyone wanted. With bit-identical weights they still
# differ by about 0.006, and decoding a quantized weight widens that to about
# 0.06. A first attempt at 0.02 failed on the third of these three, which is
# how the figure was arrived at. See docs/reference-runtime.md.
logit 0 -7.3490
logit 1 -6.9229
logit 2 8.3673
tolerance 0.08
